<title>ROMANIA: ROMANIA SIX-MONTH T-BILL YIELD RISES TO 55.01 PCT.</title>
<headline>ROMANIA SIX-MONTH T-BILL YIELD RISES TO 55.01 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield on Romanian six- month treasury bills rose slightly to an annual 55.01 percent at Wednesday's auction from 54.99 percent the previous day, central bank (BNR) data showed.</p>
<p>It said bids entered by 10 participants were double the finance ministry's offer. The discount T-bills have a 10 million lei face value and were placed through a single price auction by the BNR.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>    Total on offer		328.653 billion lei</p>
<p>    Total bids received	 664.904 billion lei</p>
<p>    Total accepted bids	 328.656 billion lei</p>
<p>    Minimum price			  73.3528 pct</p>
<p>    Maximum price			  81.5481 pct</p>
<p>    Accepted price			 78.3353 pct</p>
<p>    Annual yield			   55.01   pct</p>
<p>    Discount				 43.09   pct</p>
<p>    Maturity date		  12 Feb 1998 (182 days)</p>
<p>-- Mirela Eremia, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
